enchilada: RPMh: apps-side DDR bandwidth vote at boot (ddrbw=)

DDR looked slow to everyone: the kernel's panel copy (presentFit, 1125x2436 -> 1052x2280 BGRA)
moves ~11 MB in and ~9.6 MB out in ~9.5 ms, about 2 GB/s, and nothing in this kernel votes DDR,
so the BCMs keep whatever ABL/XBL left. Before the touch thread starts (the only other user of
the apps RSC) the kernel now sends, through the hardware-verified ACTIVE TCS path of
sweet_rpmh.c (apps RSC DRV2 0x179e0000, TCS 0x179e0d00), the vote Linux's sdm845 interconnect
driver sends for a 7216000 kBps peak, the opp-peak-kBps of the 675/710 MHz GPU OPPs and of the
top CPU OPPs, the most sdm845.dtsi asks for. CPU path acm_l3 -> qns_gnoc_memnoc -> qnm_apps
(SH5) -> qns_llcc (SH0) -> llcc_mc -> ebi (MC0, ACV); the GPU path qxm_gpu -> qns_llcc -> ebi
adds no BCM. Each BCM is looked up in cmd-db (slave 5, exactly one match, an 8-byte bcm_db aux
record) and voted as bcm_aggregate does with avg 0: vote_y = peak * width / node buswidth (32,
16, 4) * 1000 / unit, width and unit from cmd-db, clamped to 0x3fff; ACV sends its enable mask
BIT(3). Commands are BCM_TCS_CMD(commit, valid=1, x=0, y), sorted by the VCD from cmd-db, with
commit, CMD_WAIT_FOR_CMPL and a response requested only on the last BCM of each VCD
(tcs_list_gen, rpmh-rsc __tcs_buffer_write); every command must report ISSUED and those with a
response COMPLETE (tcs_tx_done) or the TCS is quarantined as before. rh_send() and rh_lookup()
take the command list and slave type for this; the ldoa28/ldoc11 path writes the same registers
and logs the same lines. The vote only goes out with rpmhrsc=0x179e0000 rpmhtcs=0x179e0d00
(SDM845); a missing BCM, a zero unit or width, or a busy TCS sends nothing. ddrbw=0 skips it.

